Move session presentation identity, mode, workspace/branch, context-source count and associated stable metadata from TuiRuntimeOptions/TuiRuntimeStateSnapshot into focused backend canonical data and a frontend projection member on TuiFrontEnd. Inventory all writers, including startup, mode changes, branch/session navigation, clear/new/resume and asynchronous completion. Publish at the authoritative backend mutation point and make initial rendering and subsequent reads use the same foo_refresh path, not separate initial-value plumbing.

Replace snapshot-based session transition detection in RuntimePresentationState and apply_runtime_state_snapshot_with_presentation_transition with a coherent frontend identity/revision transition. Preserve reset behavior for session grants, attachments, drafts, transcript/search/selection, overview and subagent views as appropriate. Transition actions belong to the tui-thread and must execute once even if rendering is coalesced; any transition with non-coalescible effects needs an explicit ordered transition contract, not just an eventually observed session ID. Results/events from the prior session must never update the new session. Do not migrate permission authority into presentation data.

Delete migrated fields and their producer/consumer assignments from the old transport in the same slice. Verify startup, repeated same-session updates, rapid session replacement, queued submit completion from the old session, failed switches and fork/clear transitions. Adapt runtime-state, prompt-stash, permission and renderer tests; run focused real terminal session-switch coverage. The remainder of the old snapshot may temporarily remain only for domains assigned to later goals.
